WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.210
It's important to remember that behind the
magic of Asgard are lots and lots of hard-working

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:05.700
people.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.360
And sometimes those hard-working people goof
up or act a little silly.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.960
It's with great pleasure that we present some
of the most hilarious Thor bloopers this side

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:14.960
of the Bifrost.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.400
"The whole thing's a f---ing mess, Taika."

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:23.300
The romantic payoff between leads is one of
the most anticipated parts of any film franchise.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.040
Actors and directors go to great lengths to
shoot and perform the most gratifying scene

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:27.540
possible.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:32.140
Thor and Jane keep coming up against all kinds
of obstacles to their love, so whenever they're

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.740
able to express their affection for each other,
it's a brief respite in the midst of world-altering

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:37.240
chaos.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.640
But it's got to be awkward to kiss your coworkers
sometimes, right?

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:45.280
Especially when you've got your trademark
long blonde Thor locks blowing into her mouth!

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:49.920
Kind of makes you wonder if that's part of
the reason for Thor keeping a short cut later

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.040
on in the timeline of the MCU.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.180
"What's that, you mouth full of hair?

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:55.660
C'mon."

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.739
This funny little snippet from The Dark World's
gag reel adds some levity to a somewhat fraught

00:01:00.739 --> 00:01:04.260
and difficult relationship, and it's nice
to see that even in the midst of something

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:08.480
so intense, Chris Hemsworth and Natalie Portman
can appreciate a little silliness.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:14.180
It seems Edna Mode from The Incredibles was
right when she insisted that superheroes shouldn't

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:14.680
wear capes.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.940
"Meta Man: express elevator.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.700
Dynaguy: snag on takeoff.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.310
Splashdown: sucked into a vortex.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:22.100
No capes!"

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:25.620
But Thor is known for his, so he would be
remiss to go without.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.590
Still, it seems to have caused a great deal
of trouble for Hemsworth, who is shown in

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:33.440
several bloopers batting the great swath of
crimson fabric out of his face.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:38.159
You would think that a weather god who frequently
summons down great winds might consider ditching

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.080
the cape and the flowing hair, but he has
an image to uphold.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:45.789
The problem any fashion-forward hero faces
is knowing that looking really cool often

00:01:45.789 --> 00:01:49.740
comes at the expense of being comfortable,
but it wouldn't do to be a god who wears a

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:50.960
windbreaker and tennis shoes.

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:52.860
No one would take him seriously!

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:57.280
Once again, this very relatable problem humanizes
one of the most powerful beings in the universe.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:03.140
In Norse mythology, the great god Odin has
two raven companions: Hugin and Munin.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.940
These elegant and intelligent birds serve
as Odin's all-seeing eyes, bringing him the

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.500
news from Midgard or Earth.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:15.800
Hugin and Munin don't have a huge role in
the MCU, but it's a nice little nod to Thor's

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.600
Norse origins to include them in a scene where
Thor has a heart-to-heart with his father,

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:18.100
Odin.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:22.180
Of course, the ravens on set are just normal
birds, even if they are more intelligent than

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:23.900
your average city pigeon.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:28.580
Trained animals aren't always easy to work
with, and ravens in particular are known to

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:30.620
be pretty independent-minded creatures.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:35.560
Instead of coming off as mystical and mysterious,
these bloopers reveal the birds to be stubborn

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:38.630
and a little hard to work with — typical
avian divas.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:43.340
Luckily, they seem to have gotten the scene
down eventually, further enveloping the viewer

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:47.810
in the magic of Asgard, but one has to wonder
if the "real" Hugin and Munin ever gave the

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.820
Allfather a hard time in the old myths.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.840
Thor and his brother Loki have a really complicated
relationship, which may have something to

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:59.150
do with the fact that Loki is a trickster
god who is never really able to stick to one

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:00.080
side of a fight.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:04.620
In Thor: The Dark World, audiences are given
a lot of screentime with the two brothers

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.030
as they work together to thwart the Dark Elves.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:10.860
Like any sibling pair, the two squabble incessantly,
even though it's obvious that they care about

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:11.880
each other.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:13.500
And then, this happens:

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:15.160
"I'm not hitting it, I'm pressing it.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:16.140
I am pressing it."

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:18.520
"You're not pressing it."

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.600
"Yes, I am."

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:25.260
Yup, that's Chris Hemsworth and Tom Hiddleston,
Thor and Loki, breaking into uncontrollable

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:25.980
giggles.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:29.220
It certainly adds depth to the brotherly love
between their characters — a brotherly love

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:33.880
that we can't help but hope extends to the
actors' off-screen friendship as well.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:38.680
In Thor: Ragnarok, Thor and Loki are introduced
to the sister they never knew they had, the

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:41.400
terrifying and all-powerful Hela, goddess
of death.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:46.890
She takes her job very seriously, sowing destruction
and misery wherever she goes.

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:51.320
It is a great blow, then, to see the equally
stunning Cate Blanchett stumble backwards

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:56.360
while unleashing some of that awesome power,
breaking the illusion of Hela's deadly poise.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:00.660
"F---."

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:05.380
It is humbling to realize that even Blanchett,
one of the most talented and elegant women

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:09.530
in Hollywood, also loses her balance in front
of lots and lots of onlookers when she's trying

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:10.860
so hard to just do her job.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:15.200
Watching her running around in a motion-capture
suit is also a bit disorienting when we recall

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:19.200
how grandiose Hela's appearance is, but a
death goddess has to do what a death goddess

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:19.820
has to do.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:25.040
It's important not to take yourself or your
job too seriously, and it seems that no group

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.940
knows this better than the cast and crew of
Thor: Ragnarok.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:33.030
Starting with the eminently witty Jeff Goldblum,
gag reel viewers are graced with several shots

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:37.290
of the actors performing fun little dances,
presumably breaking up some of the hurry-up-and-wait

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.140
monotony of a typical day on a movie set.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:43.340
The whole thing really makes you want to join
in on the fun of filmmaking, and makes you

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:47.190
anticipate watching these goofy actors in
subsequent installments within the Marvel

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:48.020
Cinematic Universe.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:50.100
Well, half of them at least.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.180
Sorry… we couldn't resist.

